    "result": "Excellent! The frai-core test suite is now fully passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Issues Found and Fixed\n\n### 1. **Missing Named Exports in Governance Module** (`src/finetune/index.js`)\nThe test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it only existed in the default export. Added named exports for:\n- `APPROVAL_STATUSES`\n- `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`\n- `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`\n- `RISK_LEVELS`\n\n### 2. **Toxicity Metric Signature Mismatch** (`src/eval/metrics.js`)\nThe `toxicityMetric` function had signature `(outputs, bannedTerms)` but was being called from `runEvaluations` with `(outputs, references)`. This caused the references array to be interpreted as banned terms, flagging all outputs as toxic. Changed the signature to `(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` to match the interface expected by the metrics pipeline.\n\n**Test Results:**\n- \u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files\n- \u2705 All public exports maintained and working\n- \u2705 No test files modified",
